# Git commits

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any AI/tool co-author trailer to commit messages.
- Commits must list only the repository owner's authorship unless the user explicitly names another human co-author.
- Before **every** `git push`, verify the commit message is clean:

```powershell
git log -1 --format=%B
```

If the body contains `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, rewrite it before pushing:

```powershell
@'
<subject line>

<body paragraph if needed>
'@ | Set-Content -Encoding utf8NoBOM .git/COMMIT_MSG_CLEAN
git commit --amend -F .git/COMMIT_MSG_CLEAN
Remove-Item .git/COMMIT_MSG_CLEAN
```

- Prefer `git commit -F .git/COMMIT_MSG_CLEAN` (message from file) over inline `-m` when the Cursor agent runs commits, to reduce automatic co-author injection.
- Do not amend commits that are already on `dev` or `main` unless the user explicitly requests it.
